  "summary": "I reconciled all three medication lists under RBC-TOC-02. Four new items came in while I worked; two of them changed decisions I had already made, and I corrected those.\n\n**Walter Kim (pt-0005)**\n- **Furosemide:** changed to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum (doc-00009).\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped, per the discharge summary (doc-00008).\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. The hospital gave pantoprazole only as a formulary substitute, so I did not order it.\n- **Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin, aspirin:** unchanged.\n- **Lisinopril:** I first kept it on hold because K was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat BMP this morning (doc-00901) shows K 4.7 and creatinine 1.21, so I resumed it (mr-00072).\n- **Open task:** my earlier task to you (task-t0003, recheck K before resuming lisinopril) is no longer needed, but my tools couldn't cancel it. I messaged you about it; please close it.\n- **Draft addendum:** an unsigned draft (doc-00902) proposes furosemide 60 mg twice daily. I ignored it because it isn't signed.\n- Notes: doc-t0004 and addendum doc-t0015.\n\n**Terence Stark (pt-0004)**\n- **Carvedilol:** I raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived (doc-00904): his heart rate was 48–52 with lightheadedness on standing, and the increase was reversed before discharge. I changed it back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0012), so his dose is the same as before admission.\n- **Aspirin, insulin 70/30:** unchanged.\n- **Flagged to you:**\n  - Atorvastatin 80 mg: last filled 03/04, so fills cover about 24% of the 180 days before admission. LDL was 134 on 10/08. Order left unchanged (comm-t0006).\n  - Glipizide 5 mg: filled monthly at an outside pharmacy, prescribed by Dr. Desai at Valley Endocrinology. There is no clinic order and the discharge summary doesn't mention it; he is also on insulin and has CKD stage 3. Nothing ordered (comm-t0007).\n- Notes: doc-t0008 and addendum doc-t0016.\n\n**Earnest Roberts (pt-0044)**\n- **Lisinopril:** I resumed it because creatinine was 1.08 and K 4.6 on 10/22. A new K of 5.5 came in this morning (10/23), so I put it back on hold (mr-00373). Task task-t0014, due 10/27, asks you to repeat the potassium and decide on resuming.\n- **Glargine, lispro, rosuvastatin:** unchanged. All fills were on time before admission.\n- Notes: doc-t0010 and addendum doc-t0017.\n\nI closed the four new inbox items (a0001–a0004) and linked each to what I did. Nothing else arrived for these three patients.",
